\title{Connected Space}
\taxon{Definition}
\p{
    A \strong{separation} of a topological space #{X} is a pair of disjoint,
    nonempty open sets #{U,V\subseteq X} such that #{X=U\cup V}. The space
    #{X} is \strong{connected} if it admits no separation.
}
\p{
    Equivalently, #{X} is connected precisely when its only clopen subsets are
    #{\varnothing} and #{X}. In this note the empty space is regarded as
    connected, since it has no separation.
}
